# PHI / PII data safety

DoctorDesk stores **protected health information** (patient names, contact, clinical notes, Rx, billing tied to care).

## Never

- Log patient content in plaintext (SOAP text, diagnoses, phone numbers in debug output).
- Send PHI to Sentry/error-tracking payloads, analytics, or LLM prompts beyond what a specific tool call strictly needs.
- Paste real patient data into agent chat, subagent tasks, or MCP calls — use seed/synthetic data locally.
- Cache PHI in `localStorage` except short-lived access tokens (prefer httpOnly cookies before prod — see Phase 19).

## Logging

- Structured logs: IDs, action keys, outcome — not chart content.
- `activity_log.summary` is human-readable but must not duplicate full clinical notes.

## AI

- Tier 2 confirm for all clinical writes and patient messages (`ai-assistant-safety.mdc`).
- Chart search tools return grounded excerpts with version IDs — never invent clinical facts.

## Files

- R2 objects are private; serve via short-lived presigned URLs only.
